## Main
To answer our research questions, we conducted a crowdsourced Many Labs project with the same translated online questionnaire given to 71,922 respondents in 68 countries on all inhabited continents (Supplementary Fig. 2). The term ‘country’ in this Article refers to both sovereign states and territories not recognized as such. The survey covered 31% of the world’s countries, which together make up 79% of the global population. The data were collected between November 2022 and August 2023, with quota samples that were weighted according to national distributions of age, gender and education level, as well as country sample size. As recommended by other studies on trust in scientists[6](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41562-024-02090-5#ref-CR6 "Wellcome Global Monitor: How Does the World Feel about Science and Health? (Wellcome, 2018);   
                  https://wellcome.org/sites/default/files/wellcome-global-monitor-2018.pdf
